WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.201
-Welcome, everybody.

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:04.804
Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show!"

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:07.874
You're here. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.976
Well, guys,
everyone is talking about this.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.578
Earlier today,
the director of the CDC

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:13.779
made a huge announcement.

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:14.848
Listen to this.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:17.817 line:0%
-Today,
CDC is updating our guidance

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:20.119 line:0%
for fully vaccinated people.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:23.623 line:0%
Anyone who is fully vaccinated
can participate

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:27.793 line:0%
in indoor and outdoor
activities, large or small,

00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:31.030 line:0%
without wearing a mask
or physical distancing.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.633 line:0%
If you are fully vaccinated,
you can start doing the things

00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:37.903 line:0%
that you had stopped doing
because of the pandemic.

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.105
-Oh, man.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.141
♪♪

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:46.813
Oh, man.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:48.581
Every bar in New York City
is going to feel like

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.518
St. Patrick's Day fell on
Cinco de Mayo.

00:00:51.518 --> 00:00:53.186
Do you know what I'm saying?

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:55.220
I think things
are about to get crazy.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.124
Seriously, I just got invited to
an orgy at Dr. Fauci's.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.794
-Really?
-Yes.

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.695
Honest to God,
the next time I hear N95,

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.430
it better be in 50 years when
I'm playing bingo.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.965
You know what I'm saying?

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.566
Everyone is excited
about the news,

00:01:07.566 --> 00:01:09.836
while the adults who
secretly got braces are like,

00:01:09.836 --> 00:01:14.140
"I thought I had more time.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:16.409
I'm just gonna wear
the mask for fun."

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:17.977
Yeah, if you are
fully vaccinated,

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:19.479
you can go back to
doing the things

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.246
you did before the pandemic.

00:01:21.246 --> 00:01:22.281
Well, not everything.

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:24.050
If you're Trump,
you still can't tweet.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:27.554
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yep.

00:01:30.122 --> 00:01:32.759
That's right -- no more masks
or social distancing

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.194
for fully vaccinated people.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:36.028
Tariq, you know what this means.

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:38.064
♪♪

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:45.705
[ Crunch! ]

00:01:48.107 --> 00:01:53.446
Slow...motion...acting.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.447
Good work, Tariq.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:55.882
As if getting vaccinated

00:01:55.882 --> 00:01:58.451
so you can return to a normal
life isn't enough incentive,

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:01.854
Ohio governor Mike DeWine
came up with a pretty bold idea.

00:02:01.854 --> 00:02:02.955
Listen to this.

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:04.857
-Governor Mike DeWine
is implementing

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:08.228
a COVID-19
vaccine incentive program

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.830
in the form of
a $1 million lottery.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.167 line:0%
Adult state residents who
have received at least one dose

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.768 line:0%
will be eligible
to win the money.

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:19.639 line:0%
A winner will be announced
each Wednesday for five weeks.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.040
-You know some idiot
is out there like,

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.910
"Yeah, but after taxes,
it comes out to only $800,000,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.578
so it's not really worth it.

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.847
I don't know."

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.648
Yeah, a million-dollar
vaccine lottery.

00:02:29.648 --> 00:02:31.917
And this is fun -- instead of
drawing from a basket,

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:33.185
they're gonna pull
numbered cotton swabs

00:02:33.185 --> 00:02:34.287
from someone's nose.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.022
-Oh, really?
-Yeah. It's a theme thing.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:37.289
-Wow!

00:02:37.289 --> 00:02:38.624
-Meanwhile,
here in New York City,

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:41.293
Shake Shack is offering
free French fries

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:43.730
to vaccinated customers,
and they made the announcement

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.965
during Mayor Bill de Blasio's
briefing.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.133
Let's see how that went.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.701
-Show us your vaccine card,

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.803
we'll get you
a free fries on us.

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:54.907
-Free fries
when you get vaccinated?

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:56.809
You're saying I can get this?

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:59.445
These delicious fries?

00:02:59.445 --> 00:03:00.713
If this is appealing to you,

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.815
just think of this
when you think of vaccination.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.551
-Ugh!
-Mmm!

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:07.887
Vaccination. Mmm!

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.122
[ Laughter ]
-Ugh!

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:11.357
-Wait.

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:13.026
-Wait.
-Oh, my God.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:15.028
-Wait a minute.
-Oh! Oh!

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.795
-The sound you just heard
was every New Yorker

00:03:16.795 --> 00:03:20.399
puking and then packing
for Ohio.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:21.400
-Oh, my God.
-Wait.

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:23.236
-Somehow, that was real.

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.603
-That was real?
-Yeah, it happened today.

00:03:24.603 --> 00:03:26.872
-Can I get de-vaccinated?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:27.973
-That wasn't you guys?

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:29.008
-No.
-No.

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:30.076
No, that was actually --
That happened.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.578
-That was real. That happened.
-Yeah.

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:34.680
-Somehow,
de Blasio did the impossible.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.516
He made people want to
stop eating French fries.

00:03:37.516 --> 00:03:41.654
I'll go get a third dose
if he stops eating on camera.

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:42.688
Some news out of Washington.

00:03:42.688 --> 00:03:43.856
Yesterday, President Biden

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.326
met with the big four leaders
of Congress.

00:03:46.326 --> 00:03:47.827
And I thought some of
the things he had to say

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:48.995
were pretty interesting.

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.263
-Hmm.
-Take a look.

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.814
-What?
-Wow! A muskie?

00:04:08.814 --> 00:04:10.350
-I don't know what
he's talking about.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.517
That wasn't all that he said.
-Wow!

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.753
Really? He said more?
-Yeah, he said this.

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:33.039
-What is he talking about?

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:35.040
-Wow!
-Why doesn't anyone stop him?

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:37.076
-Yeah, he's the president.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:38.143
-And, finally,
he had this to say.

00:04:38.143 --> 00:04:39.379
-Are you serious?
One more thing?

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.047
-Yeah, we -- Listen to this.

00:05:00.132 --> 00:05:01.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.602
-What?
-I don't know.

00:05:03.602 --> 00:05:05.604
You know, it seems like
the country is going through

00:05:05.604 --> 00:05:07.240
a different shortage every day.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.007
This week,
it started with gasoline.

00:05:09.007 --> 00:05:11.243
And now it's something
even more serious.

00:05:11.243 --> 00:05:13.379
Chick-fil-A
has a sauce shortage.

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:14.780
-Oh!

00:05:14.780 --> 00:05:19.719
-Dear God, will those Russian
hackers stop at nothing?

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:20.720
Don't worry.

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.221
We just made a deal with
Saudi Arabia

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.824
for 10 million barrels of honey
mustard, so we're all good.

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:27.059
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.059 --> 00:05:28.093
Beep-beep!

00:05:28.093 --> 00:05:29.661
The milkman will let you
honk the horn.

00:05:29.661 --> 00:05:31.230
-Oogah!
-Yeah.

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.432
[ Car horn honks ]

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:36.402
-Here's some more
poultry-adjacent news.

00:05:38.737 --> 00:05:41.841
KFC is making some changes
to its packaging.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.542 line:0%
KFC is changing its packaging.

00:05:43.542 --> 00:05:45.010 line:0%
It's adding instructions
on their buckets

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.145 line:0%
for reheating leftovers.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:47.346 line:0%
-Oh.

00:05:47.346 --> 00:05:49.649
-Yeah. People who eat KFC
were like, "Leftovers?

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:57.556
I just keep going till
my fist hits cardboard."

00:05:57.556 --> 00:05:59.092
-Boom!
-Yeah.

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:00.759
-KFC is redoing their packaging.

00:06:00.759 --> 00:06:03.228
When asked why, they said
it was on their bucket list.

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:04.229
[ Audience groans ]

00:06:04.229 --> 00:06:06.065
[ Rimshot ]
What?

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:08.000
How -- Our show is canceled?
-Come on.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.170
-Our show is canceled
that fast, from that?

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.739
Can I finish the monologue?

00:06:13.739 --> 00:06:15.441
It's just a couple more jokes.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:17.409
We're off the air?

00:06:17.409 --> 00:06:18.978
You got to be kidding me.
Well, I had a good run.

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.046
Love you guys.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:22.081
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:33.493 --> 00:06:36.028
-Bucket list.
-Aha!

00:06:36.028 --> 00:06:37.329
This is the bucket-list show.

00:06:37.329 --> 00:06:38.564
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:40.032
-Well, guys,
it's now been over a year

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:42.501
since we all got on Zoom,
and, yet, some people

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:43.869
are still getting
the hang of it,

00:06:43.869 --> 00:06:45.004
even people on the news.

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.072
So you know what that means.

00:06:46.072 --> 00:06:47.606
It's time for another
installment of

00:06:47.606 --> 00:06:49.708
"Greatest Moments in
Zoom History."

00:06:49.708 --> 00:06:50.709
Enjoy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:54.247
♪♪

00:06:54.247 --> 00:07:00.619 line:0%
-My baby walked over
a mat in the --

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:01.821 line:0%
-Did we lose Bill?

00:07:01.821 --> 00:07:03.255 line:0%
Uh-oh. Poor connection.

00:07:03.255 --> 00:07:04.389 line:0%
-What made you want to do it?

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:06.759 line:0%
-Well, my mom presented
the idea to me,

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:10.962 line:0%
and she said that I could be
one of the first --

00:07:10.962 --> 00:07:12.464 line:0%
-I think we just lost Ty.

00:07:12.464 --> 00:07:15.668 line:0%
Ty, I think we have you back,
so I'll ask the question again.

00:07:15.668 --> 00:07:17.637 line:0%
What made you want to be
a part of this trial?

00:07:21.673 --> 00:07:24.577 line:0%
-And, John, in the early days
of this investigation,

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:26.078 line:0%
what stands out to you the most?

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:30.449 line:0%
-One-two, one-two, one-two,
one-two, one-two, one-two.

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.552 line:0%
One, two, three, four, five --
-We can hear you, John.

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:35.521 line:0%
-So, let's see if
we can give Theresa a call.

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:36.522 line:0%
-Hello?!

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.790 line:0%
-Theresa!
-Theresa!

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:40.593 line:0%
-You're upside down, girl.

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:43.028 line:0%
Will you flip
your phone upside down?

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:44.530 line:0%
-We can't see you.
-This way?

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.933 line:0%
-One more. One more click.
-One more.

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:47.934 line:0%
One more.

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:48.934 line:0%
-One more.
-One more.

00:07:48.934 --> 00:07:49.936 line:0%
-One more.

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:51.403 line:0%
Yeah!

00:07:51.403 --> 00:07:53.973
-That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:53.973 --> 00:07:56.275
You got it.

00:07:56.275 --> 00:07:57.810 line:0%
And, finally,
it was just announced

00:07:57.810 --> 00:08:02.882 line:0%
that the "Friends" reunion
will air on HBO Max on May 27th.

00:08:02.882 --> 00:08:05.584
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:05.584 --> 00:08:09.255
May 27th?
"Could it be any closer?"

00:08:09.255 --> 00:08:10.890
Yep, they're calling it
"The Episode" --

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.124
They're calling the episode

00:08:12.124 --> 00:08:13.693
"The One that Costs
Way More than the Others."

